Z||000002||mbramble||07-31-2001||10:53 AM||||The thread topic says '84' but your first post asks about putting it into an '86'??  I'm not sure about the 84's as I keep hearing about the wiring, etc., differences between them and other years (though I suspect it will plug right in).  But you should have no problems plugging it into an 86 -- well except for the fact that the tach will be off since it came out of 6 cyl and you are putting into a 4.  I just did a search for 'tach 4 6' in the Tech Archives and came up with several threads but it was unclear to me if you can make the 6 cyl unit work properly in a 4 cyl car.  Also, I don't know if 86's had the wiring harness for the aux guages built in like the 87/88's did.  If not, there is a thread that batboy posted about how to add the wiring harness at <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000815-2-001538.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000815-2-001538.html</A> <p>[This message has been edited by mbramble (edited 07-31-2001).]||||reg||1
